{
  "$comment": "Single source for the built-in price table in all three SDKs. Edit this file, then run `python3 scripts/gen_pricing.py` to regenerate packages/sdk-go/pricing_table_gen.go, packages/sdk-node/src/core/pricing-table.ts and packages/sdk-python/rateguard/core/pricing_table.py. CI fails if they drift, if a row is past its priceChangesOn date, or if the table has not been reviewed for more than 90 days. Prices are USD per 1M tokens, standard (not batch, not priority) tier, read off the vendor page in sourceUrl on seenAt. Cache-read discounts are not modelled, so an estimate for a heavily cached prompt lands above the invoice. Llama via Groq is not tabled: Groq publishes no on-demand price for it (\"Contact sales\" on 2026-10-14).",
